# Planned city upgrade validation

Require construction-plan cities to upgrade an owned settlement.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] A planned city is valid on an existing settlement belonging to the selected player.
- [ ] A planned city is valid on that player's settlement created by an earlier valid plan step.
- [ ] A planned city is invalid on an empty vertex, an existing city, or another player's settlement.
- [ ] An invalid city attempt does not append or mutate any plan step or real Board state.
- [ ] Preview projection upgrades the settlement to a ghost city without retaining a duplicate settlement.
- [ ] Board edit-mode building cycling remains unchanged unless separately required.
- [ ] Invalid attempts use TASK-019's shared 1.5-second lower-screen feedback.
- [ ] Analytical domain tests and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Ordered projection must validate against the Board plus all earlier accepted plan steps.
